# Entirely fictional incident summaries; no real people, locations or case identifiers.
# Categories describe reports, not proven offences or findings of guilt.
# One item per line. Blank lines and lines starting with '#' are ignored.
Shop staff report seeing a person conceal packaged goods in a bag and leave without paying.
A witness reports that an unattended bicycle was taken from a public cycle rack without the owner's permission.
A passenger reports that someone took their bag from a station bench and ran away.
Store staff report that a customer carried a boxed appliance past the tills and left without payment.
A business reports that someone forced entry into its locked office overnight and removed several laptops.
A resident reports a rear door was forced open while they were away and jewellery was taken from inside.
A caretaker reports that a locked storeroom was entered through a broken window and tools were removed.
A witness reports an attempted forced entry into a closed shop; the person said they intended to steal stock before leaving.
A witness reports seeing a person deliberately spray paint across a shop's shutters.
A parked vehicle's owner reports seeing someone deliberately scratch its doors with a metal object.
A caretaker reports that someone intentionally smashed the windows of a bus shelter and walked away.
A resident reports that a person deliberately kicked down their garden fence without trying to enter a building.
A company reports paying an invoice after someone falsely claimed to be its regular supplier and supplied a different bank account.
A buyer reports that a seller took payment for a laptop advertised as genuine but knowingly sent an empty box.
A resident reports transferring money to a caller who falsely claimed to work for their bank.
A business reports that a caller impersonated its manager to obtain a payment for a fabricated urgent order.
Officers receive reports of a person shouting threats at passers-by in a town square.
Station staff report an individual directing threatening abuse at travellers and refusing to stop.
A witness reports a group surrounding pedestrians and shouting threats in a public shopping area.
Bus staff report that a person at the stop was threatening other passengers and aggressively blocking their path.
A caller cannot find their wallet and does not know whether it was lost, left at home or taken.
A shop reports a cracked window but has no information about how or when it happened.
A resident reports loud music from a nearby property, with no threats, damage or other details.
A caller says there was an incident near the park but provides no description of what occurred.
